7. Gate ingestion writes behind pre-flight validation and rework result shape

    [x] 'content/backend/core/engine_deps/result.py': Rework IngestApplyResult
        - replace written / deleted / errors with six fields:
          created, updated, deleted, missing_paths, unexpected_paths, parse_errors
        - happy-path lists are empty whenever any error list is non-empty, and vice versa
        - all-or-nothing contract: no partial results

    [x] 'content/backend/asset_ingestion/ingestion_service.py': Add pre-flight validation to apply_file_changes
        - after parsing, reject (no disk ops) if parsed.errors is non-empty
        - verify every create path does NOT exist → collect failures into unexpected_paths
        - verify every update path DOES exist → collect failures into missing_paths
        - verify every delete path DOES exist → collect failures into missing_paths
        - existence checks via get_file_contents, catching NoSuchFile
        - if any check fails, return result with only the relevant error list(s) populated
        - if all checks pass, perform disk ops; populate the matching happy-path list
        - keep per-item try/except around actual writes/deletes for runtime surprises (permission, etc.)

    [x] 'content/backend/controller.py': Adapt ingest handler to new result shape
        - replace manual dict construction with dataclasses.asdict(result)
        - response JSON keys now match the six field names directly
        - no more bundling creates+updates into 'written'
        - 200 when all error lists are empty (job done)
        - 400 when any of parse_errors / missing_paths / unexpected_paths is non-empty (rejected, no disk ops)
        - 500 on unhandled server-side exception (permission denied, disk failure, etc.)

    [x] Subtask: align the JS SPA to handle the new response shape
        - ingest response now carries created / updated / deleted / missing_paths / unexpected_paths / parse_errors
        - UI must render distinct feedback for each category rather than a single written/errors pair
        - 400 responses surface the specific error lists to the user for correction
        - 500 responses treated as server failure (alert / retry)